Falsifies `system_tests::user::address_wait_tests::the_reserved_address_wait_forms_and_foreign_words_are_refused`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect: the address wait methods of milestone 812 (`std::thread::spawn` runs real threads in one
address space) admit every flags word, so a shared address wait and a 64-bit address wait, both of which §269
(how threads share a process) reserves, are served as if they were the private 32-bit form.

Expected to fail: "a shared address wait was not refused as a form this kernel does not answer", which
gets `NotPermitted` from the next check instead of `BadMethod`.

diff --git a/kernel/src/system_call/address_space.rs b/kernel/src/system_call/address_space.rs
index dbfda40aa..0dc3f6c74 100644
--- a/kernel/src/system_call/address_space.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/system_call/address_space.rs
@@ -249,9 +249,6 @@ fn address_space_address_wait(
     flags: u64,
     word: u64,
 ) -> Result<i64, Error> {
-    if !moho_abi::address_wait::is_admitted(flags) {
-        return Err(Error::BadMethod);
-    }
     if !rights.allows(Rights::READ) {
         return Err(Error::NotPermitted);
     }
